// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3202762397" "You did a good thing today, {HeroName}. I guess it's easy to see how Crey could have disregarded the wishes of Number 6; to them, it was just a product they'd made. But I'm proud to be working with a hero who can't ignore any living being in trouble."
// RandomFameString :
"P1253079145" "There's this wild weblog by this guy called Number 6 who says he's a free-willed A.I. Ain't that crazy?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1175308340" "I know you tried, {HeroName}. We can hope that the AI program found a way to free itself before it was reprogrammed, but the truth is, we may never know."
// RandomFameString :
"P940369927" "I hear good AI is just around the corner. Crey's been making some really good strides in that direction."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL6_Crey_Errand1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2220139979" "I can't believe Crey is doing this, {HeroName}. There are people in Founders' Falls and Brickstown, people outfitted as Crey security force members, harassing people and performing combat drills on the streets. The countess denies any knowledge or authorization of this activity, but says that she can't do anything to stop them until they're brought in and she can uncover the conspiracy. Not that any of them ever talk. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Whether these people are Crey or not, they have to be stopped.</A> Can I count on you to help?"
// AcceptString :
"P1118388809" "Fight 'Crey' agents"
// SendOffString :
"P2503953097" "If these people are rogues, then defeating them will only help improve relations between Crey Industries and the city in general. And if they're not rogues... Well, it might be a good idea to learn how to fight them."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2810124748" "Combat Crey menace"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P822852812" "It doesn't matter where you go to fight these guys, {HeroName}, as long as you beat them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2742571421" "You have defeated enough Crey operatives for the moment."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3839177856" "The countess is once again thanking you for all of your hard work fighting corruption, {HeroName}. The 'rogue' Crey operatives you brought in aren't talking, though. You have to wonder if the countess is in control at all with these kinds of problems in her own company."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL6_Crey_Errand2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3367129788" "Crey's Folly was declared a hazard zone and walled off during the early stages of reconstruction. Whatever Crey was working on out there, it ruined the whole area when the Rikti blew it up. As a hazard zone, it's supposed to be off-limits to non-authorized entry, but Crey has been performing salvage operations out there anyway. And all the trouble they stir up keeps coming right back into the city.<A HREF={ACCEPT}>Crey's Salvage operations out in Crey's Folly are illegal and need to be stopped.</A> And the only way to do that is to bring Crey operatives to justice in that zone."
// AcceptString :
"P1161050826" "Fight Crey Operatives in Crey's Folly to disrupt illegal salvage"
// SendOffString :
"P3020912082" "Though Crey's lawyers are trying to tangle the whole thing up in court, right now Crey's salvage operations are illegal, and pose a threat to the city at large. They've been seen out in Tangle Town and the old Paragon Water Works, but anywhere you can catch them should still help."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3761748615" "Defeat Crey in Crey's Folly"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2643302566" "Go to Crey's Folly and defeat Crey operatives to disrupt their salvage operations, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3187473403" "You have cleared out enough Crey to impede their salvage operations."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4144185260" "The final fate of Crey's Folly is going to be tied up in courts for years, {HeroName}, but they can't be allowed to take advantage of that to endanger the rest of the city. If heroes like you can keep up the pressure, they just might take the hint about that one day."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL6_Crey_Errand3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P61144878" "Ziggursky Prison in Brickstown is where a lot of extremely dangerous people are kept incarcerated. Council Cor Leonis, Circle mystics, Freakshow, and worse. The security systems in there are top of the line, and then need to remain at peak effectiveness. That's where the problem is. Crey has been testing out new field equipment for its agents, and it seems to be having some odd side effects. One of them is playing havoc with Ziggursky security. Crey has refused to acknowledge the problem, and meanwhile prisoners are taking advantage and escaping. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>If Crey won't stop their street tests on their own, then I'd like you to shut them down.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P2587024145" "Shut down Crey on the streets of Brickstown"
// SendOffString :
"P2343204372" "Crey has been pretty unfriendly towards heroes lately, {HeroName}, so it's unlikely that they'll just stop when you tell them to. You can probably find them around Mashu Bridge and the Crescent, but don't limit yourself to just those areas."
